    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my realtor just told me i need to set up an escrow account for the house i'm buying in toronto. whats that actually is and why do i need it for the closing?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "An escrow account, in this case, is a separate bank account that holds funds for the down payment and closing costs of your new home. It's like a little \"goblin's treasure chest\" where your realtor can stash the money until the closing date, when it's needed to finalize the transaction. Think of it as a temporary holding cell for your down payment, keeping it safe from prying eyes, just like a goblin might stash its loot in a hidden cave.\n\nNow, why do you need it? Well, the escrow account is used to hold the down payment and closing costs until the closing date. This way, the funds are not released until the transaction is complete, ensuring that the seller receives the full amount and you get the keys to your new home. It's a bit like a goblin's promise to keep its treasure safe until the right moment to reveal it – in this case, the closing date.\n\nIn Toronto, the escrow account is typically held by a third-party escrow agent, who will manage the funds and release them according to the terms of the sale. Your realtor will work with the escrow agent to ensure that the funds are transferred correctly and on time. So, to summarize",
